				<tr>				
					<td bgColor=#c7b19c valign=top align=right nowrap width="10%">
					<b><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2">Bio:&nbsp;</font></b>
					</td>	
					<td bgColor=#c7b19c valign=top>
					<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Gartrin was born in the great city of Freeport to a set of commoners, his father was a boat builder and his mother stayed with gartrin throughout his younger years. During the early years gartrin went to the docks to watch the great war boats being built for the journey over seas. For a war was being waged in a far away land against lizard like creatures, many of his fathers friends went over seas and few came back with stories that gartrin was never allowed to hear but he listened closely at night from his bed. It was quite by accident that gartrin learned the ways of illusion. When he was but a young teenager he happened upon a road show, for that year the faire was in town and he met a young lass by the name of Kayla, she sat with him fishing and talking about how this enchanter was teaching her how to turn into different things, and make beasts her friend. Gartrin laughed and told her that she couldn't do these things "for we are only common folk, and magik was reserved for the noble class of citizen". She looked at him and then looked at an alley cat walking close by. Her hands began to glow and a slight crackling of hot air could be heard. Suddenly the cat walked upto her and sat next to her meowing and purring at her side. Gartrin knew well that most of the cats in the city were wild and not to be interfered with. Gartin began his training in secret the next week. Four years later the sea side of freeport was threatened, reports of a ship carrying Iskars warriors was approaching, the local guards assembled to met any threat that landed while powerful magik users lined the shores awaiting their targets. A war never did ensue but it so scared gartrin that he traveled to the local guild and took the entrance test to hone his megar skills into a true art of magik. It was Tergok Manifoot that took a interest in Gartrin after he was turned down by the guild, gartrin knew he was turned away because the blood he had running through his veins was common, not noble. Tergok saw that gartrin had a true interest in the art and with the proper training could be a master illusionist in time. Targot also knew it was that very thing that the guild feared and quickly turned gartrin away for fear of having a non noble class be, a better class of enchanter, for it was the rumor that commoners might be dangerious if given power. Targok quickly took gartrin under his wing and taught him to the 16th season, what took most trainies five years to complete, gartrin did in three. Gartrin emerged a young but powerful enchanter, dispit his mother and fathers pleas not to continue. In the end however gartrins family was there when he left to a land far away, and one that was wrecked by recently ended wars.  When gartrin returned five years later he found that his father had died in his sleep the year before, since, his mother had taken ill, poor and barally able to care for his younger sister and herself. Gartrin immediately had a house built in north freeport and deposited the remainder of his treasures put in an account for his mother. He made sure that she and his sister would be well taken care of. There he stayed until his sister was married to a knight, it was a happy time for her and the family but with all happiness comes sorrow. The next day his mother died. Gartrin was devistated, he took a long walk that day after the burial and happened into a young battle torn barbarian by the name of Whacha, the barbarian could see that gartrin was down on his luck and offered to by him an ale. There they sat watching the market place sell its wares. After a time of talking gartrin was asked if he wished to do some traveling and see the world. Gartrin's face lit up at the possibilities and he knew he had no ties in freeport any longer. His friends all with families, or off adventuring. The next week they were off. So begins the saga of gartin, so ends this entry in my log.</font>
